From 177a650aee493fe1484a62e1ae5a7c52d8b14ae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kobbler-Media <dev@kobbler.invalid>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 14:49:53 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] server: LLAMA_WORKER_ISOLATION parent/child split +
 /v1/admin/{drain,load,unload}

Re-graft of the one non-perf kobbler patch that upstream lacks, required before
the vanilla-tip build can replace the turboquant prod image (koblem-llama).

WHY: koblibs kob-gpu-gate lets avatar/video jobs borrow the GPU from the LLM.
That requires the LLM to release ALL its VRAM on demand and reclaim it later.
A single-process llama-server cannot: the CUDA primary context is never torn
down until the process exits. Solution: a CUDA-free parent that owns the HTTP
port and fork+execv's a child holding the model + GPU. POST /v1/admin/unload
SIGKILLs the child -> primary context teardown -> all VRAM returned to the card.

DESIGN: opt-in via env LLAMA_WORKER_ISOLATION=1 (child sees
LLAMA_WORKER_ISOLATION_CHILD=1 and runs as a normal single-process server, so
the hot path is byte-identical to upstream). The parent rebinds every
model-facing route to a proxy through the child (server_http_proxy, the same
SSE-relay primitive the router server uses), so it transparently exposes the
FULL upstream API on top of which it adds the admin lifecycle endpoints:
  - POST /v1/admin/drain  -> 503 new requests; in-flight streams finish
  - POST /v1/admin/unload -> SIGKILL child, reclaim all VRAM (idempotent)
  - POST /v1/admin/load   -> lazy pre-warm + clear drain flag
/health stays parent-side and reports {loaded,busy,draining,in_flight} for the
kob-gpu-gate drain loop. Per-request GPU placement via X-Worker-Gpu header /
WORKER_DEFAULT_GPU env (index or GPU-UUID). Heavy inference endpoints are
drain-gated + in_flight-counted + lazy-spawning; metadata/tokenizer/stream
endpoints proxy without gating and never re-fork an evicted worker.

GPU-VALIDATED on RTX 3060 (2026-07-14): parent idle 130 MiB (CUDA-free);
first chat lazy-spawns child (7543 MiB); /props + /v1/models proxied; drain
returns 503; unload drops VRAM 7543 -> 130 MiB (fully reclaimed);
load/next-request re-spawns; legacy /admin/* aliases work; child logs relayed.

Ported from the turboquant fork (hbd-llama-cpp-turboquant, worker_isolation.*
+ server.cpp hooks) and adapted to upstream's split server.cpp / server_routes
(the fork's unrelated post_control/*_tok/count_tokens deltas are already
upstream and were NOT re-applied).
